## 0) Executive summary

In Phase 3, our team extends the reliable data transfer system from Phase 2 into a full **RDT 3.0 stop-and-wait protocol** over UDP. The major addition in this phase is support for **packet loss recovery**, while preserving the Phase 2 handling for **bit corruption** through checksums, sequence numbers, and ACK-based retransmission behavior. Our sender includes a retransmission timer so it recovers from both lost DATA packets and lost ACK packets, which is the defining feature of RDT 3.0. The receiver remains logically aligned with the RDT 2.2 receiver, meaning it accepts only the expected sequence number, discards corrupted or unexpected packets, and sends the most recent valid ACK when needed. We validate completion of this phase through three methods: functional demo scenarios, byte-for-byte file verification between sent and received files, and performance experiments that measure average file transfer completion time across all five required options from 0% to 95% error/loss in 5% increments. The resulting CSV files and plots are included in the repository under `results/`. This phase is complete because the protocol correctly transfers a file under all required scenarios and produces repeatable experiment outputs.

